    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and all tests pass. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `locality` field is derived from the owner's city and returned in the owner JSON, matching the established pattern for derived owner fields (`membershipTier`, `householdId`, etc.). Three files touched:\n\n1. **`Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper: `Locality.of(city)` looks up the fixed table `Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`, returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(Locality.of(owner.getCity()))\")` line on `toOwnerDto`.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 one `locality` property added to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** the derivation lives entirely in the new cohesive `Locality` class (its own `of` method has WMC_other \u2248 0, CC 1). The only edit to existing code is a single annotation line on the abstract `toOwnerDto` method (CC 1, low surrounding complexity), so no existing method grows in complexity. No function bodies were changed \u2014 the whole feature is added as a small new unit.",
